# Drafted by Gemini (R15 village_after), edited.

~ adela_cure
Narrator: Adela peels back the long kidskin glove one button at a time, and the hand beneath it is pink, warm, and entirely whole.
adela_druskenvald [sad]: Oh, mercy. For a month I have smelled river mud every time I unpinned my sleeves, and now it is simply my own hand again.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Forgive me, a lady ought not to go to pieces in the parlour. Here is every coin I promised you for riding down into that dreadful sink.
set adela_cured
gold +150 each
if flag.adela_secret_kept
adela_druskenvald [smile]: And this second purse is for your discretion. Not a soul in the manor has looked crookedly at my gloves, and I am in your debt.
gold +50 each
endif
quest withered_arm done
-> adela_ring_menu

~ adela_ring_menu
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Is there anything else before I ring for fresh tea, my dears?
* [if item:adelas_wedding_ring] Return her wedding ring -> ring_return
* [if item:adelas_wedding_ring] Keep her ring for ourselves -> ring_keep
* Tell her what the Grinning Sinner truly was -> adela_told
* Take our leave -> END

~ ring_return
Narrator: Her fingers tremble so badly that the gold band clicks against her knuckle twice before it settles into its old groove.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: I told Phillip it was at the jeweller's having the clasp tightened. You have saved more than my arm tonight, and I will not forget it.
take adelas_wedding_ring
set adela_ring = "returned"
gold +25 each
inspiration party
-> adela_ring_menu

~ ring_keep
Narrator: Her gaze lingers a beat too long on the familiar band of gold before she folds her bare hands neatly in her lap.
adela_druskenvald [weary]: Keep it, then, as the price of a foolish woman's vanity. A jeweller in town can copy the filigree before Phillip thinks to ask.
set adela_ring = "kept"
-> adela_ring_menu

~ adela_told
adela_druskenvald [afraid]: Please, spare me the particulars of his coffins and his debts. I already see that dreadful scaly smile whenever the hearth fire burns low.
adela_druskenvald [weary]: Only promise me that Phillip never hears how closely my little bargain brushed against his name. He has burden enough keeping this valley upright.
-> adela_ring_menu
